review='docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/GPT_DIVINATION_RANK1_SOURCE_CONFERENCE.md'
minute="In initiative, expires at the caster's tenth future regular-start marker after application; outside initiative, expires 60 elapsed seconds after application. Preserve the virtual phase or absolute deadline through initiative changes, absence, death and planar travel. An already-passed start never counts."
hour="Expires 3,600 elapsed seconds after application, regardless of initiative changes, absence, death or planar travel."
common=" Actual class access, repertoire, V/S/F components, costs, Dissonance/Refrain, beginning hooks, concentration transitions and interruption follow SPELL_INTEGRATION_RULES.md. Costs commit before the counter window without refunds or restoration of prior concentration. Explicit remote-destination/concealment exceptions override ordinary originating line of effect only as printed. Specific information protections apply to their actual subject and generating-source scope; hidden but unprotected facts are valid information, and missing facts are never invented. No automatic scaling or upcast."
replace=" A successful replacement owns its new endpoint; stale cleanup cannot remove it. A failed or countered cast creates no replacement, although an applicable concentration transition has already happened."
guard=" Mark Omen and Fate Coin share one guard: an original roll event and its entire replacement lineage may receive at most one reroll from either of these two spells, across all casters, coins, marks and recasts. Reserve this allowance at the first legal activation's commitment, not after the replacement die resolves. For a multi-die roll, the whole set/pool is one original roll event; the resulting attack's separate later damage roll is a different event. A shared area-damage roll remains one event even when applied to several creatures. Other exact class reroll features keep their own permissions and timing, but do not erase this guard or create a fresh lineage for these two spells. If competing declarations are simultaneous, use current initiative order; outside initiative use a fixed neutral table order chosen before the roll. Only the first legal commitment spends a mark/coin; a later declaration barred by this guard spends nothing. No new Action, roll event, cast, payment or duplicated outcome hook is created by replacing dice."
cards=[]
def add(id,ran,targets,duration,conc,resolution,effect,limits,notes):
 s=src[id];cards.append({'id':id,'activation':'Action','rangeFeet':ran,'targets':targets,'duration':duration,'concentration':conc,'components':['V','S','F'],'resolution':resolution,'effect':effect,'scaling':'None. No automatic increase in targets, range, duration, uses or information.','limitations':limits+common,'designNotes':notes,'implementationStatus':'LOCAL CANDIDATE — source-reconciled; exact manuscript review pending; not selectable','sourcePlacements':s['sourcePlacements'],'sourceCoreEntries':s['sourceCoreEntries'],'classAccessEvidence':s['classAccess'],'sourceReview':[review],'reviewEvidence':[]})

add('true-sight-lesser',0,'Self; creatures within 30 feet on your plane.','1 minute, no concentration. '+minute,False,
 'No roll or additional scanning Action. For the duration you can actually see creatures in the area despite Invisible, Hidden or ordinary non-solid visual obscurity, including darkness, smoke, mist and foliage.',
 'This magical sight reveals the creature itself sufficiently for ordinary sight-dependent targeting. It ends Hidden from you and removes Invisible’s own unseen attack modifiers for you under the current Core known-position exception. Solid opaque barriers and total cover still block the view. Blindness or another effect expressly preventing your sight still applies. Other cover and independent obstructions retain whatever effect this sight does not actually overcome. Protection from Scrying can withhold new Divination-derived sight of its protected creature, but does not conceal a creature your ordinary senses can already see.',
 'Only you gain this sense. You may communicate what you perceive through ordinary means; allies gain neither magical sight nor automatic identification. It supplies no true-form/disguise detection, Ethereal sight, alignment, hidden-object search, general illusion revelation or creature statistics. Once a position has been learned, spell expiry does not erase that knowledge or automatically reestablish Hidden; later actual hiding and ordinary sensory changes use the existing rules. One active True Sight (Lesser) per caster; successful recasting replaces it.'+replace,
 'PRESERVED: Action/V,S,F, one-minute sight of invisible/hidden creatures without concentration. CONFLICT RULING: raw 30-foot metadata becomes a 30-foot sensing radius for a Self beneficiary. NEW: exact non-solid-obscurity/solid-cover boundary, passive sight and observer-specific consequences.')

add('warning-ward',30,'One point on solid ground or a suitable immobile surface that you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect.','Concentration, up to 1 minute. '+minute+' Ends earlier with concentration; no glow survives the ward.',True,
 'No roll. At each actual outside-to-inside entry, the Director determines whether that creature has an actual current hostile relationship toward you in the encounter/campaign state. A qualifying entry starts or refreshes the visible signal for 6 elapsed seconds from that entry, capped by the ward’s own endpoint.',
 'Place one faintly visible magical sigil watching a fixed area 10 feet in radius and 10 feet high above its surface. Qualifying hostility may be secret if it is an actual current fictional fact; do not infer it from species, alignment, faction, reputation, appearance or suspicion. Undefined hostility does not become hostile merely to trigger the spell. Entry includes voluntary movement, forced movement and teleportation that actually occupies the area. Creation around an already-present creature is not entry; it must leave and reenter. Ordinary intervening cover within the area does not prevent physical entry from triggering, but a protection blocking the creature’s new Divination information can prevent its trigger. During a signal the mark is self-luminous and visible under ordinary line-of-sight rules; it does not illuminate surrounding squares. Its only direct report is that at least one qualifying entry occurred recently. Repeated entries refresh the same signal, without separate counted pulses or a stored log.',
 'One Warning Ward per caster. The area stays fixed; moving or destroying its supporting surface ends the ward rather than making a portable detector. Ending concentration or suppressing the ward prevents new signals and removes its visible glow; suppression does not pause the ward’s duration or replay missed entries when it ends. A formerly signaled entry is not a new entry just because suppression ends. No damage, restraint, sound alarm, creature outline, square, count, identity, type, statistics or detailed intention is reported. Actual observers can make ordinary inferences from the glow and its timing.'+replace,
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/concentration1minute, a trap glowing on enemy entry and no damage; Core M/F follows shared F interpretation. NEW: fixed 10-foot-radius/height region, actual-hostility predicate, no trigger on creation, and signal lasting exactly 6 elapsed seconds rather than an ambiguous turn marker. Exact-card completion specifies self-luminous-only signal, ordinary-cover entry behavior, suppression and moved-surface endings.')

add('scribe-destiny',30,'One creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect. Choose greatest desire or greatest fear before its save.','Instantaneous',False,
 'The target makes a Wisdom save against your spell DC. On success you learn nothing. On failure privately learn one actual currently dominant deep desire or fear in the chosen category, subject to specific information protection.',
 'The result is an intelligible concept, not necessarily a verbal quotation, and does not require a shared language. It is a fundamental motive rather than only the creature’s passing mood. When several motives are genuinely coequal, the Director records one consistent selection while the materially relevant state remains unchanged; repeat casts do not rotate through tied motives. A genuinely absent motive in the chosen category reports None discernible. An undefined or specifically protected answer reports Indeterminate. Creature type alone does not decide whether a motive exists: an active Undead or Construct can qualify when its actual mental state supports the answer.',
 'This supplies no Frightened condition, emotional compulsion, guaranteed leverage, automatic check success, memory search, truth verification or future behavior. Immunity only to Frightened is not an immunity to reading a fear; an actual defense covering mental/divinatory information retains its exact scope. The spell adds no voluntary-save waiver, automatic notification of success/failure or future-cast immunity. Ordinary perception of casting and actual defensive features may reveal the attempt.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F/instantaneous, greatest desire or fear and WIS save. NEW: caster category selection, intelligible deep-motive output, stable tie handling and independent absence/undefined/protected results; Fear tag grants no condition.')

add('mark-omen',30,'One creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect; creature type alone adds no exclusion.','Up to 1 hour, until consumed; no concentration. '+hour+' Ends earlier when the marked creature dies, is destroyed or its summoned existence ends.',False,
 'No initial save. Once while the mark lasts, when you make an attack against that creature, you may consume the mark after the complete initial attack d20 result is visible but before hit/miss resolution. This costs no additional Action or Reaction. Replace the entire attack d20 procedure using the original modifiers and advantage/disadvantage state; use the replacement result even if worse.',
 'The mark is invisible and nonphysical. A two-d20 advantage/disadvantage attack receives a complete new two-d20 set and the ordinary higher/lower selection; a single-d20 attack receives one new d20. Do not reroll damage or modifiers. Resolve natural 1, natural 20, expanded critical eligibility and the hit/miss result only from the final attack result under their actual rules. The attack must already be legal under its own range, sight and line-of-effect requirements; the mark adds no continuing 30-foot tether, tracking information or new targeting permission. One active Mark Omen per caster; a successful new mark replaces the old one. Different casters can independently mark a creature for their own attacks.',
 'Ordinary shapechange retaining creature identity does not remove the mark. Actual death, destruction or ended summoned existence ends it; revival/reconstruction/resummoning does not revive that application. Information-only protection does not itself cancel this noninformational reroll permission. No ammo, RP, component, class use or other original attack cost is refunded or charged again, and the replaced result produces no separate hit/miss/on-hit outcome. A legally committed mark stays spent if an exact later interrupt prevents completion.'+guard+replace,
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F, one attack reroll against a marked creature within one hour. CONFLICT RULING: finite one-hour pending mark replaces Instantaneous metadata. NEW: caster’s own attack only, no extra action/reaction, full d20-set replacement before hit/miss, fixed lineage guard shared only with Fate Coin and creature-identity endings.')

add('clairaudience-lesser',5280,'One specific fixed known location within 1 mile on your plane; only you receive the hearing. You must have personally visited it or have a reliable map/description identifying that particular location.','1 minute, no concentration. '+minute,False,
 'No roll. Create a fixed nonphysical auditory sensing point at the chosen known location. No originating sight or line of effect to that distant point is required. The point cannot be placed inside solid matter; an invalid location gives no hearing and refunds no committed cost.',
 'You hear from the point according to ordinary sound conditions there: local walls, soundproofing, silence, speaker distance and volume all matter. You continue hearing your own surroundings normally at the same time. Deafened prevents receipt of remote audio while it applies. Maintain a same-plane, 1-mile tether between you and the fixed point; leaving it suppresses remote hearing without ending or pausing the spell, and returning while time remains restores only current audio, not a backlog. Specific Divination protection can withhold new information about its subject while leaving unprotected ambient sounds available. The point is an ongoing magical effect that may be detected or ended only by another effect whose actual targeting, range and permissions apply; it has no physical body or HP.',
 'One sensing point from this spell per caster; successful recasting replaces it. It cannot move, pan, follow a surface/creature or search for an unknown place. It supplies no vision, language translation, voice authentication, replay, recording, remote attack, casting through the point or originating line of effect for another ability. Ordinary ambient silence is not proof of an empty room, and a blocked read reveals no reason. The point is not a creature, object, scout, summoned ear, portable token or loot. Duration continues during suppression.'+replace,
 'PRESERVED: Action/V,S,F, hearing a distant known location for one minute without concentration. CONFLICT RULING: NEW functional range1mile replaces raw30feet to fulfill the distant-site promise. NEW: fixed nonphysical point, simultaneous ordinary hearing, Deafened/tether suppression, one-caster limit and no solid-matter placement.')

add('fate-coin',30,'Your free hand or the free hand of one willing creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect.','Up to 1 hour, until expended or destroyed; no concentration. '+hour,False,
 'Conjure one noncurrency Tiny magical coin, AC10/HP1, mass0.01pound. A current holder with a usable hand may flip and expend it as a Reaction after one eligible die face is visible but before the roll’s mechanical consequences are applied. There is no separate heads/tails success test. The coin vanishes and its use commits when the legal Reaction begins.',
 'The holder must perceive the creature/object generating the roll or the actual local event being resolved, within 30 feet and line of effect. Physical tabletop dice location is irrelevant. The roll can belong to the holder, an ally or an enemy; no target consent is required. Its result must actually be available to the reacting player under the table’s normal information rules; the coin does not reveal secret rolls or fabricate perception. Choose one physical die from that original roll. Reroll only it and use the new face: for two-d20 advantage/disadvantage reselect the higher/lower normally; for a multi-die damage, healing or resource pool recompute the original total; for a single-die attack/check/save use its new face. All original modifiers, other dice, target selection and source rules remain. If the roll is shared across targets, use the same modified shared result for all of them. An initial Resonance Well reserve d4 may be changed before the reserve is established, but an already established reserve cannot be rerolled or refilled.',
 'One active Fate Coin per caster; successful recasting replaces the previous unspent coin wherever it is. Ordinary handing/dropping/custody and hands apply; a handoff never refreshes the charge, endpoint or caster cap. The spell adds no separate one-coin-per-holder cap: several casters may supply distinct coins, still constrained by actual hands, Reactions and the shared roll guard. At0HP, expiry or replacement, this conjured coin vanishes without creating material; it is not currency, sellable stock or a component. Its native HP is not an Integrity conversion. Ordinary Reaction prohibitions apply. A prevented committed use is not refunded. No already-resolved hit, HP loss, healing, RP grant/transfer, cost or completed outcome can be reversed. The spell grants no character-generation rewrite, out-of-fiction table control, automatic access to hidden Director dice or extra reroll of the entire pool.'+guard+replace,
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet, once during next hour flip coin to reroll any one die, Core M/F mapped to F. CONFLICT RULING: finite one-hour physical token replaces Instantaneous metadata. NEW: Reaction/30foot perceived-event interface, one mandatory replacement face, one caster coin, shared Mark Omen/Fate Coin roll-lineage guard. Exact-card mass0.01lb quantifies the source conference’s negligible weight for carrying; AC10/HP1 are native object values.')

add('detect-secret-doors',0,'Self; concealed passage entrances within 30 feet on your plane.','Instantaneous',False,
 'No roll. Privately learn the precise position and boundary of each actual qualifying concealed passage entrance in range, subject to specific Divination protections.',
 'Qualifying features include secret doors, hidden trapdoors, movable concealed panels, hidden passage openings and comparable intentionally concealed entrances. Ordinary walls, paneling, masonry, furniture and visual concealment do not block this specific entry-detection procedure. An actual entrance hidden by an illusion can be revealed without granting knowledge of unrelated illusion properties. The detection can identify an entrance behind an intervening ordinary wall if that entrance itself is within30feet; it does not require the caster already to see its concealing surface.',
 'It reveals the entry, not a map of the passage network or rooms beyond it. A buried tunnel without a qualifying entrance in range is not mapped merely for passing nearby. No door or tunnel is created where the fiction has none. There is no unlocking, opening, trap detection/disarming, knowledge of a trigger mechanism, construction history, route beyond range, treasure report or persistent public outline. The knowledge is an instantaneous private spatial snapshot, not tracking or sight through all surrounding matter.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/V,S,F/instantaneous and reveal hidden passages within30feet. NEW: Self-centered30foot range, precise concealed-entry boundary and explicit ordinary-concealment bypass limited to that information. Specific anti-Divination protection still applies; general dungeon mapping is not granted.')

add('faction-insight',30,'One creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect. Choose one exact canonical factionId you know.','Instantaneous',False,
 'No save. Privately learn the target’s actual current standing score for that faction, plus the corresponding standing category only if current canonical faction data defines one. Undefined or specifically protected information reports Indeterminate.',
 'Director-held hidden standing is legitimate information when unprotected. Use the actual current record and current reputation authority, normally -3 through+3 under REPUTATION.md. The absence of an established standing record is not zero. If a numeric score is known but no canonical category is defined, report that score without inventing a title.',
 'This supplies no membership, loyalty, intentions, institutional rank, credential, legal authority, prices, social history or other faction standings. No save or positive-standing caster gate is added. It changes no reputation and does not import the historical -5..+5 scale. Creature type alone does not exclude an actual creature with a standing record; the record may be part of established Director fiction rather than a software character file.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F/instantaneous and standing with one faction. NEW: exact known-faction selection, actual numeric/category output, missing/protected Indeterminate and creature eligibility without biological restriction.')

add('alignment-sense',30,'One creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect.','Instantaneous',False,
 'No save. Privately report the target’s actual current canonical Lawful/Neutral/Chaotic and Good/Neutral/Evil axes. Unprotected Director-held values are revealed. Each undefined or specifically protected axis independently reports Indeterminate.',
 'A known axis remains reportable when the other is unknown or protected, unless the actual protection covers both. Exact masking effects may alter an output only within their written permission. Do not infer an axis from ancestry, species, faction, reputation, faith, appearance, oath or a stereotype.',
 'No object targeting, extra targets, extended aura, ward bypass, personality/intent reading, crime record, truth detector, allegiance, future behavior or alignment change. This intentionally keeps the source’s rank-1 price and creature-only target despite overlap with rank-0 Sense Alignment. Relative value remains an open balance/source-cleanup issue; neither card is quietly rewritten to justify the price.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F/instantaneous and exact alignment of one creature. NEW: explicit two-axis records, independent Indeterminate results and private snapshot. The overlap with Sense Alignment is recorded, not hidden with an unprinted power increase.')

add('resonance-map',0,'Self; active magical-energy records within 30 feet, on the same plane and in line of effect.','Instantaneous',False,
 'No roll. Receive one private spatial snapshot of qualifying magical-energy concentrations: their current locations and actual footprints/extents within the sensing area. Ordinary total cover excludes the blocked portion.',
 'Qualifying sources are actual active spell effects, magical zones/fields, active auras and magical objects/effects with active magical-energy records. Where a source has an actual comparable source-defined magnitude, rank or intensity, represent that actual value; without a comparable value, show presence and extent without inventing power units or relative ranking. Multiple eligible footprints can overlap in the snapshot without being collapsed into a fabricated total strength. A mere RP pool is not itself an active aura unless its own source says so. The map can reveal an otherwise unseen magical effect’s position. If an unprotected attached aura gives away a Hidden/Invisible creature’s location, ordinary known-location consequences follow, but this spell does not grant sight of that creature’s body.',
 'The footprint is clipped to the permitted sensing area; it does not map an entire distant effect merely because one edge is nearby. Information protection on a creature cannot be bypassed by relabeling its attached magic as independent; genuinely independent environmental magic remains separately eligible. No automatic spell name, owner, alignment, faction, charges, recipe, RP amount, harvest right, spell control or permanent map item. It does not track later movement or drain/recover energy. Remembering or writing the permitted snapshot uses ordinary memory and tools.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/V,S,F/instantaneous and magical-energy concentrations in an area. NEW: Self-centered30-foot same-plane/LoE spatial snapshot, actual footprint clipping, comparable recorded intensity only and explicit distinction from RP-pool sight.')

add('read-memories',30,'One willing creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect, consenting to share one specific memory or sufficiently narrow topic.','Instantaneous compressed memory experience',False,
 'No save. Confirm willingness at cast start and again at resolution. The recipient selects an actual remembered episode satisfying the agreed specific consent. You experience up to one continuous minute of that episode through its remembered perspective. If consent is withdrawn or the memory does not exist, transfer nothing and refund no committed costs.',
 'The recipient identifies the start of the selected continuous interval as part of consenting; you cannot silently append other memories or move to another topic. Receive the remembered sensory and subjective experience, including whatever the recipient actually remembers rather than an external reconstruction. Mistaken, incomplete, altered, implanted or biased memories remain such. Speech is experienced as remembered, with no independent translation of an unfamiliar language. An active Undead or Construct can qualify when it has actual memories and can willingly consent. An unconscious creature cannot supply current willing consent merely through someone else’s assertion.',
 'Specific information protection can prevent new information from its protected subject even when that subject consents; willingness alone does not waive Protection from Scrying. This neither verifies objective history nor reveals facts absent from the memory. No forced reading, memory deletion/editing, persistent recording object, skill/proficiency download, completed crafting/research action, altered elapsed clock or free project progress. A later cast can share a different actually consented memory normally; no daily cap is added.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F/instantaneous and one specific memory from a willing creature. NEW: particular-topic consent at start/resolution, recipient-selected continuous interval up to1minute, subjective compressed experience and no automatic translation/objective verification.')

add('corruption-insight',30,'One creature you perceive within 30 feet and line of effect; alternatively, a fixed10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you perceive within30feet and line of effect.','Instantaneous',False,
 'No save. Examine one current qualifying Corruption record and privately report its actual type and proximate causal source. The two fields independently report Indeterminate when undefined or specifically protected. Report No Corruption only when no actual Corruption is present and no relevant protection prevents determining that fact.',
 'Creature mode examines Corruption actually affecting that creature. Area mode examines environmental Corruption belonging to the selected area itself, within the sphere and line of effect to its center; it does not inspect every occupant merely for standing there. Type means the actual recorded category, type or name. Source means the immediate established cause responsible for that record, such as a spell, curse, artifact, creature effect, site or environmental source. An explicit Corrupted condition can supply that actual type, but does not by itself invent who or what caused it. If the caster already distinguishes a qualifying current record, they may select it. Otherwise the Director uses a fixed deterministic order recorded for those applications before answering; materially unchanged repeat casts return that record rather than rotating through hidden applications. A distinct known record can be selected on a later cast.',
 'Do not extrapolate an immediate cause into an upstream conspirator, current owner/controller location, complete history or unknown actor identity. A source actor protected against the information cannot be exposed merely through its causal association; report the permissible cause/type fields without the protected detail. Undefined data is not proof of absence. No new numeric Corruption track, save DC, full statistics, cure, cleansing, alignment report, poison/disease/species inference, suppression or harvest permission. The spell supplies information only.',
 'PRESERVED: Action/30feet/V,S,F/instantaneous and source/type of Corruption affecting a creature or area. NEW:10-foot environmental-area mode, one-record deterministic selection, proximate-source meaning, independent known/protected fields and clipped center-LoE. Existing Corrupted definition is evidence, not a new universal cause or taxonomy.')

assert len(cards)==12
candidate={'status':'LOCAL CANDIDATE — SOURCE-RECONCILED; exact manuscript review pending; NOT SELECTABLE','scope':'Twelve rank-1 Divination identities; twelve placements/Core blocks and exact six-class access preserved. Authored tabletop procedures; runtime, numerical balance and broader-domain closure remain open.','reviewEvidence':[review],'spells':cards}
p=D/'candidate_divination_rank1.json';assert not p.exists();p.write_text(json.dumps(candidate,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n',encoding='utf-8');digest=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
intro='''# Twelve rank-1 Divination spells — exact manuscript review

Please review all twelve exact cards against your source conference and existing shared rules. Approve or provide exact required repairs. The catalog remains 170 reviewed / 678 unfinished until approval; all twelve original placements/Core blocks and actual class access are retained. This is manuscript review, not runtime, numerical balance or whole-game certification. Please keep the response below 17,000 characters.

These exact completions need particular attention:

- Warning Ward uses your actual-hostility predicate, including secret but established hostility. Its fixed 10-foot-radius/10-foot-high region triggers on outside-to-inside entry even through ordinary intervening cover, matching Alarm Ward's physical-entry treatment; actual Divination protection can still prevent the protected subject supplying the trigger. The mark is self-luminous only, not a surrounding light source. Each entry starts/refreshes exactly six elapsed seconds of glow, capped by ward expiry; this specific signal uses elapsed time rather than an ambiguous caster-start round marker. Moving/destroying its support ends it; suppression stops signals and provides no replay of missed entries. Please approve these exact completions or repair them.
- Mark Omen and Fate Coin reserve the shared original-roll-event guard at activation commitment. A whole multi-die pool/set is one event; a subsequent attack damage roll is a different event. A shared area roll stays one event across all targets. Other class rerolls retain their own rules but cannot reset this lineage. Simultaneous competing declarations use current initiative order, or a fixed neutral table order set before the roll outside initiative. Only the first legal commitment spends a mark/coin. This priority applies only to these two spell grants, not a new universal interrupt system.
- Mark Omen remains caster's own attack, no extra action/reaction, full d20-set reroll before hit/miss, no new30-foot use tether. Death/destruction/ended summoned existence ends it; not creature type or ordinary shapechange.
- Fate Coin quantifies your negligible mass as NEW0.01lb for actual carrying, AC10/HP1, not currency. It must be in a usable hand to flip as a Reaction. No separate one-coin-per-holder limit was added because your conference only specified one per caster; actual hands, Reaction and original-roll guard still apply. Its range anchor is the perceived generating creature/object or actual local event, not the gaming dice. The result must be available under ordinary table information rules; no secret-roll revelation. Any eligible die, including a Well's initial reserve before establishment, can be changed. Modified shared rolls stay shared. No refunds if a committed activation is later actually prevented.
- Clairaudience's functional range is5280feet and the caster alone receives audio; raw30feet remains source evidence. Point must be a particular known location, not inside solid matter, with no originating sight/LoE requirement. One caster point, ongoing nonphysical magic effect detectable/dispellable only under actual other-source permissions, no HP object. Same-plane1mile tether/Deafened suppress only the hearing, preserving clocks and no backlog.
- Detect Secret Doors follows your explicit ordinary-matter bypass: an entrance itself within30feet can be revealed even behind an intervening ordinary wall. No whole tunnel layout, opening or trap information is added. True Sight separately sees creatures through non-solid obscurity but never solid total cover, and does not remove Blindness.
- Scribe Destiny supplies one deep conceptual motive, not fear condition or biological assumption. Faction/Alignment readings retain actual records and unknown/protected outputs. Alignment Sense's rank1 redundancy with Sense Alignment remains an open balance issue.
- Resonance Map clips footprints to the readable30-foot area, represents comparable recorded magnitude only, and does not treat every RP pool as a magical aura. It may reveal an unprotected aura's location without granting sight of its attached creature.
- Read Memories uses a recipient-selected start of an actual consented continuous episode up to1minute; willing memory-sharing cannot automatically waive information protection. Different later memories remain available through new legal paid casts.
- Corruption Insight's area mode reads environmental Corruption, clipped by line of effect to the selected center, not every occupant's private state. Existing Corrupted condition evidence below supplies a possible actual type, but no invented causal source. The Director records a stable record order; unknown extra records cannot be sampled by unchanged recasts. Protected causal actor details remain protected independently of an otherwise reportable cause/type.

Please identify any conditional approval and its exact changes. If approved, I will add the Mark Omen/Fate Coin guard as an explicit shared spell overlay without editing frozen class rules. Broader roll-interrupt, perception, travel, information, faction and Corruption systems remain open.

## Exact candidate

'''
fence=chr(96)*3
packet=intro+'Candidate byte SHA256: '+digest+'\n\n'+fence+'json\n'+json.dumps(candidate,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n'+fence+'\n'
ev=read(A/'DIVINATION_RANK1_CORRUPTED_CONDITION_EVIDENCE.json');packet+='\n## Existing Corrupted condition evidence\n\n'+fence+'json\n'+json.dumps(ev,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n'+fence+'\n'
pp=A/'CODEX_DIVINATION_RANK1_EXACT_REVIEW.md';assert not pp.exists();pp.write_text(packet,encoding='utf-8')
sub={'status':'prepared for exact review; not promoted','ids':list(src),'candidatePath':str(p),'candidateSha256BeforeReview':digest,'packetPath':str(pp),'packetSha256':hashlib.sha256(pp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'operationalBefore':170,'unfinishedBefore':678}
(A/'DIVINATION_RANK1_EXACT_SUBMISSION.json').write_text(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8');print(json.dumps({'count':12,'packetCharacters':len(packet),'candidateSha256':digest},indent=2))
